Title: Boxes and ids
Author: Reebeat tests

/* A small original story for the core tests: two Sections, four Scenes,
   one cut and two auto-animated Scenes. */

# The same box

= One box, two screens.

INT. FIRST SCREEN

A box {#box @tl .box}
The caption {#cap @bc .muted hidden}
Old news {#old @mr .label}
Footer {#foot @bl .muted}

NARRATOR
(slowly)
This box sits in the corner. [[next]] The caption says what it is.

NARRATOR
Look at the box. [[focus: box]] [[sfx: pop]]

> AUTO-ANIMATE

INT. SECOND SCREEN

A box {#box @mc .box .accent}
The new caption {#cap @bc .muted}
New arrival {#new @tr .title hidden}
Footer {#foot @bl .muted}

NARRATOR
(pause 0.5)
Same id, new place. [[sfx: whoosh]] [[next]] A new element enters.

# The cut

> CUT

INT. THIRD SCREEN

/* a note that is not a Cue */

Fresh start {#fresh @mc .title}

NARRATOR
(quickly)
Nothing is matched across a cut.

> AUTO-ANIMATE

INT. FOURTH SCREEN

Fresh start {#fresh @tc .title}

NARRATOR
[[sfx: ding]] The title moves up.
